# User wording does not shorten triggered bot waits

These phrases do **not** waive wait gate (step 5) or thread closure (step 6) in **`WORKFLOW.md`** / **`git-pr-workflow-default.mdc`**:

- "Merge everything" / "batch merge" / "land the queue"
- "Just merge" / "urgency" / frustration tone
- "CI green" / "checks passed" while threads are missing or unsettled
- Skipping dynamic bot wait (`wait-for-bots` exit 0) after creating a new PR or after tagging bots

**Code changes alone do not start a new wait cycle.** Only creating a new PR or tagging bots (`--bot-tag`) starts a new wait anchor. Only an explicit written waiver for that specific PR waives bot closeout.

Full ship bar: **`WORKFLOW.md`**.
